[{"id":2918973153,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6t-_7h","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","login":"kitbdev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev"},"body":"When the limit rect is enabled, it defaults to a high value for each so you cannot see the limits. There is no background color for it either, so it is not visibile in the 2d editor until the limits are changed. This is fine and you may not want to set all 4 to be in visible range. The issue is clicking inside of the limit rect it only moves it and other nodes cannot be selected, which by default will be everything in your scene.\r\nSo, I think the limits should only be movable from the edges, its fine to only allow moving the limits individually IMO. Diagonal dragging would help too. This way we can just return false in gui_input and allow other nodes to be selected.\r\n\r\n\r\nChanging the limits in the inspector when typing or using the up down arrows doesn't update the limits in the 2d editor until it is redrawn.\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: Also this fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107409","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104190#pullrequestreview-2918973153","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104190","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-12T00:02:48Z"},{"id":2920501109,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6uE091","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19a2a4ff85&v=